      "Subject": "URGENT: Rotterdam DC scanning system down, trucks waiting",
      "Body": "All handheld scanners in the Rotterdam DC lost connection 20 minutes ago. Outbound loading has stopped and we have six trucks waiting at the dock. We need someone on this within the hour or we miss today's cutoff.",
      "Category": "Network",
      "Priority": "Critical",
      "Rationale": "The issue affects all handheld scanners at a distribution center and has stopped outbound loading, indicating broad operational blockage, so Critical is appropriate. The closest KB article only provides service desk contact/severity information and does not include scanner-specific troubleshooting, so the reply escalates rather than inventing a fix. Confidence is moderate because the classification is clear but the KB lacks a direct article for this system.",
      "Confidence": 0.72,
      "Draftreply": "High business impact: Hi Dave,We understand that all handheld scanners in the Rotterdam DC lost connection, outbound loading has stopped, and trucks are waiting at the dock.The knowledge base does not provide a scanner-specific recovery procedure for this issue, so we are escalating this to a specialist for urgent investigation rather than giving you unsupported steps.For live follow-up, the Service Desk can be reached at extension 4357 (HELP), staffed 06:00\u201320:00 local time, Monday to Saturday. The Rotterdam DC lobby walk-up desk is also available during business hours.Thank you for flagging the business impact clearly.HomeFix Supply Support Team. "
